# SRG-APP-000224-WSR-000137  -  CAT II
# The web server must generate a session ID long enough that it cannot be
# guessed through brute force.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000224-WSR-000137
group:           V-206401
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-001188
control_rev5:    SC-23

contribution:    Splunk Enterprise generates session identifiers internally and exposes no
                 setting for their length; the session settings in web.conf govern only
                 whether session support is on, when a session expires, and how the session
                 store is held. There is accordingly no configuration value for the
                 application to set toward a minimum identifier length.

external:        The length in bits of a generated session identifier - a fixed property of
                 Splunk Enterprise's session subsystem; establish it by inspecting an
                 issued session cookie or by vendor attestation from Splunk
external:        Any session identifier substituted by a fronting reverse proxy or SSO
                 component - that component's configuration

manual_reason:   Session identifier length is fixed by the product's session subsystem.
                 web.conf.spec exposes tools.sessions.on, tools.sessions.timeout,
                 tools.sessions.restart_persist, tools.sessions.storage_type and the cookie
                 attribute settings, and none of them bears on the number of bits in a
                 generated identifier. Writing a condition over any of them would test
                 something that does not decide the requirement.

citation:        web.conf.spec:920-983 (the complete set of tools.sessions.* settings: on,
                 timeout, restart_persist, httponly, secure, forceSecure, storage_type,
                 storage_path - no length or strength setting among them)
finding:         Not decidable from Splunk configuration: the product exposes no session
                 identifier length setting, so the application's share of this requirement
                 is satisfied by product design and the identifier length must be
                 established by inspecting an issued cookie or by vendor attestation.
